MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_001: Majesty! You never do fail to impress.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_002: I was mesmerized during the war-council meeting.\nYou really won everyone over. It was inspiring!
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_003: We need allies willing to take a stand. I will not allow\nthe world to share Damascar's fate.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_004: Damascar's fate... Now there's a story. Do you know\nof the last voyage of Vandahl, Swashbuckler King?
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_005: Vandahl? What has your father to do with\nDamascar?
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_006: Well, he was seduced by a beautiful woman, and\nthey went to the Isle of Sorrows, you see...
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_007: But it turned out the Isle of Sorrows was the tomb\nof Balor—and Vandahl's blood broke the tomb's seal.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_008: Then he took the treasures from inside, the pieces of\nBalor's corpse, and gave them all to his wife, Maria.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_009: So it was your father who opened the tomb?\nWhile Damascar took the blame.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_010: That's right. He played with fire, and Damascar got\nburned... Does that change how you feel about me?
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_011: I have no strong feelings toward either you or\nyour father.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_012: Really? Here I expected you to take a swing...
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_013: Why waste my time with this idle chatter? I doubt\nyou mean to apologize for your father's folly.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_014: Oh, no, I'm not apologizing for him. He was living\nhis life as an adventurer, and these things happen.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_015: I have my own feelings on the matter, sure, but...
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_016: I was curious how your opinion of me might change,\nknowing all that.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_017: For a merchant to take the measure of a queen\nrequires some gall.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_018: Your father was a convenient excuse for the Divine\nEmperor to do what he longed to.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_019: Yu Phas blessed Damascar with her love. Dagda\nresented this and sought to see it razed.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_020: If there is an unforgivable figure in this story, it is he.\nThough he is now food for worms.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_021: Hm. So justice has been served, then.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_022: Yet others would take up his power and bring ruin\nto the land again, dragging all of Dagda into it.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_023: That is why I have taken spear in hand alongside the\nmighty warriors of Saramis.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_024: We will slay Balor and restore peace to the world.\nI would have your aid in this, Talimun.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_025: I thought you'd have lost some of your spark in these\nfive years, but you've still got it, Majesty.
MID_SE_Seo_Tal_B_026: Alright, you sold me. We're going to accomplish\ngreat things together.
